questions.question_text:
A boat sails directly away from the foot $A$ of a vertical cliff at $2$ m/s.
The top of the cliff is $C$, $20$ metres above $A$, and the boat is at $B$, $x$ metres from $A$.
The angle of depression of the boat from $C$ is $\theta=\arctan\dfrac{20}{x}$.
At what rate is $\theta$ changing when $x=20$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0,3);
\coordinate (B) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (H) at (2,3);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (C) node[midway, left] {$20$ m};
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$x$ m};
\draw (C) -- (B);
\draw[dashed] (C) -- (H);
\draw ($(A)!0.3cm!(C)$) -- ($($(A)!0.3cm!(C)$)!0.3cm!90:(A)$) -- ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\pic[draw, angle radius=1.1cm, angle eccentricity=1.35, "$\theta$"] {angle=B--C--H};
\node[above left] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
